  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was strong operationally but surfaces a divergence between your two locations that needs attention.\n\nPort Washington ran at $531 per groomer\u20146% above baseline\u2014with five groomers on floor producing an 18% revenue jump. The standout: retail up 80% and add-on attach jumping from 35% to 54%. This is real execution. You're also seeing early retention lift; the 12+ week visit-gap bucket contracted 2.2 points, suggesting customers are coming back sooner. Week-to-date is up 20%. July MTD sits 2.3% below expectation on a DOW-adjusted basis\u2014essentially flat performance; the headline \"down 2%\" is calendar noise, not a miss.\n\nHicksville tells a different story. Add-on revenue fell 32% despite core grooms up 26%, and retail dropped 14%. Productivity per groomer hit $448, above the $419 baseline, but that's masking a upsell discipline problem\u2014your team is executing the groom but not attaching services. More concerning: Hicksville's 12+ week bucket grew 2.4 points, a leading indicator of stealth churn. MTD is flat (actually +7.4% DOW-adjusted), but the visit-cadence drift suggests you're treading water. Inventory depletion on X-Small Treat Table is severe (-140 units); restock immediately.\n\nThe pattern: Port Washington is firing on all cylinders; Hicksville needs focus on attachment training and customer retention messaging. Both locations have critical retail stock-outs that are likely leaving money on the table.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Today you've got 10 groomer-days scheduled (7 Port, 3 Hicksville) with 7.0h bather coverage at Port; next 7 days total 50 groomer-days (34 Port, 16 Hicksville) at 43.0h bather hours\u2014Port is weighted for volume, Hicksville is light.**"
